From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:09:16 -0400
Subject: feat: the hidden sidebar's rest and the sidebar's speed as settings

GitHub issue 45, its first idea. "Show a hidden sidebar" sets the rest at
the window's edge before a hidden sidebar slides in: at once, 0.05, 0.1
(the default), 0.25 or 0.5 seconds, and 0.2 seconds more at the right
edge, where the page's scroll bar is; both of the reveal's timers read it.
"Sidebar animation" runs the sidebar's collapse, expand, hover overlay,
hidden slide and Space slide at Normal, Fast (half the time) or Instant:
the animation controller scales the clock's run of a motion, so every
keyframe keeps its place. "Hover delay" gains 0.25 and 0.5 seconds. Each
has a Settings row and a cycling command bar row.

Why: GitHub issue 45; the owner said yes on 2026-10-27 and asked on
2026-11-01 for it to be built here.
Removable when: never as a feature; the controller hunk goes if Chromium
gives its browser animations a speed of its own.
